    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <section class="py-32 px-6 md:px-12 bg-white text-brand-dark border-t border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-[1000px] mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tighter mb-16 uppercase gsap-reveal">FAQ's</h2>

            <div class="border-t border-gray-200">
                <!-- Q1 -->
                <div class="gsap-reveal border-b border-gray-200 faq-item group">
                    <button
                        class="w-full text-left py-6 font-bold text-base md:text-xl flex justify-between items-center interactive focus:outline-none tracking-tight pr-4">
                        How is this different from hiring a PR agency and a separate consultant?
                        <svg class="w-6 h-6 transform transition-transform duration-300 icon text-gray-400 group-hover:text-black shrink-0 ml-4"
                            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7">
                            </path>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="pb-6 text-gray-600 font-medium text-base leading-relaxed hidden answer">
                        Normally you would brief several vendors and stitch their output together yourself. Here, one
                        team holds the full narrative, so your press materials, leadership content and employer
                        messaging never pull in different directions.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q2 -->
                <div class="gsap-reveal border-b border-gray-200 faq-item group">
                    <button
                        class="w-full text-left py-6 font-bold text-base md:text-xl flex justify-between items-center interactive focus:outline-none tracking-tight pr-4">
                        We worked with an agency that only sent out press releases. How is this different?
                        <svg class="w-6 h-6 transform transition-transform duration-300 icon text-gray-400 group-hover:text-black shrink-0 ml-4"
                            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7">
                            </path>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="pb-6 text-gray-600 font-medium text-base leading-relaxed hidden answer">
                        A press release is one tactic, not a strategy. We start with an audit and a narrative, and every
                        piece of PR or content ties back to it. Activity is never the point. Visibility and trust are.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q3 -->
                <div class="gsap-reveal border-b border-gray-200 faq-item group">
                    <button
                        class="w-full text-left py-6 font-bold text-base md:text-xl flex justify-between items-center interactive focus:outline-none tracking-tight pr-4">
                        Do you handle crisis communication?
                        <svg class="w-6 h-6 transform transition-transform duration-300 icon text-gray-400 group-hover:text-black shrink-0 ml-4"
                            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7">
                            </path>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="pb-6 text-gray-600 font-medium text-base leading-relaxed hidden answer">
                        Yes. Crisis-readiness and response planning sit inside corporate communications, so you are not
                        writing a plan for the first time in the middle of a problem.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q4 -->
                <div class="gsap-reveal border-b border-gray-200 faq-item group">
                    <button
                        class="w-full text-left py-6 font-bold text-base md:text-xl flex justify-between items-center interactive focus:outline-none tracking-tight pr-4">
                        Is this only for large companies?
                        <svg class="w-6 h-6 transform transition-transform duration-300 icon text-gray-400 group-hover:text-black shrink-0 ml-4"
                            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7">
                            </path>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="pb-6 text-gray-600 font-medium text-base leading-relaxed hidden answer">
                        No. Founder-led and growth-stage companies benefit the moment their messaging starts reaching
                        media, investors or a growing team in inconsistent ways.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q5 -->
                <div class="gsap-reveal border-b border-gray-200 faq-item group">
                    <button
                        class="w-full text-left py-6 font-bold text-base md:text-xl flex justify-between items-center interactive focus:outline-none tracking-tight pr-4">
                        Is this a retainer or a one-off project?
                        <svg class="w-6 h-6 transform transition-transform duration-300 icon text-gray-400 group-hover:text-black shrink-0 ml-4"
                            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7">
                            </path>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="pb-6 text-gray-600 font-medium text-base leading-relaxed hidden answer">
                        Most reputation work runs on a monthly retainer, because consistency is what builds trust over
                        time. Specific pushes, like a launch or a single campaign, can be scoped on their own.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q6 -->
                <div class="gsap-reveal border-b border-gray-200 faq-item group">
                    <button
                        class="w-full text-left py-6 font-bold text-base md:text-xl flex justify-between items-center interactive focus:outline-none tracking-tight pr-4">
                        How soon will we see results?
                        <svg class="w-6 h-6 transform transition-transform duration-300 icon text-gray-400 group-hover:text-black shrink-0 ml-4"
                            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7">
                            </path>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="pb-6 text-gray-600 font-medium text-base leading-relaxed hidden answer">
                        First coverage and first bylines usually land within 60 to 90 days. Reputation compounds, so the
                        strongest results tend to show over 6 to 12 months.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
